 "attribution": {
  "B/C, every item": "the item-off run already differs by +7 to +14 % (harmonized-v1-isotopic): DRAGON2's fixed helium target multiplies every production cross section by 1.144-1.174 (He_to_H_CS_ratio, ported in the test as he_to_h_ratio); after dividing it out DRAGON2 / closed form is 0.93-1.01 (residual: helium on destruction, DRAGON2's own inelastic cross sections, 2D gas and boundary; not separated). The item effect (diagnostic) agrees within 0.7 % (convection) and 0.13 % (decay)",
  "10Be/9Be, decay": "the closed form is a thin disc; DRAGON2's gas layer at the observer (H2 59 pc, HI 115 pc) is comparable with the 10Be decay length sqrt(D gamma tau_0) of about 0.3 kpc at 0.1 GeV/n, so fewer 10Be produced off the mid-plane survive to z = 0. A 1D finite-difference diagnostic with the source on DRAGON2's gas profile against the same column in a thin disc gives a surviving-fraction ratio F(E) that matches the DRAGON2 item effect within 1 % in the bins at 0.08-0.2 GeV/n; the lowest bin (0.05-0.078 GeV/n: DRAGON2 effect 0.969, F 0.816) and a +1 % residual above 1 GeV/n are not attributed",
